WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:03.170
- Mm-hmm. All right.
Hey, palsies!

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:05.380
My name is Cody,
and I'm a Helpster.

00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:07.341
That means a monster who helps.

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:10.886
And because I love, love, love
to help so much,

00:00:10.969 --> 00:00:12.930
I'm making these videos called...

00:00:17.309 --> 00:00:20.145
There are so many people
helping us right now,

00:00:20.229 --> 00:00:23.690
and I wish there was a way
we could say thank you to all of 'em.

00:00:23.774 --> 00:00:28.862
Well, guess what?
There are so many ways!

00:00:28.946 --> 00:00:31.615
You could write a letter,
or send a card or a drawing,

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:34.701
or you can make a video
like I'm doing right now.

00:00:34.785 --> 00:00:37.287
Or you could sing them a song.

00:00:37.371 --> 00:00:40.791
And you could get
some friends to help, like...

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.292
Grouplove!

00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:44.753
- GROUPLOVE: Hey!

00:00:44.837 --> 00:00:46.630
- Hey, Grouplove!

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:49.174
Hey, you got your instruments
all ready to make some music?

00:00:49.258 --> 00:00:51.426
- No. No, we don't.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.679
- What? No? But-but-but-but--

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:56.682
- We thought we'd loop sounds
to make music instead.

00:00:56.765 --> 00:00:58.183
Right, everybody?

00:00:58.267 --> 00:00:59.434
- Yeah!
- Yeah.

00:00:59.518 --> 00:01:03.063
- Ah! I love that idea!

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:05.357
You know, my friends and I
loop sounds all the time.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.943
Oh, loop means
to do something again and again.

00:01:08.026 --> 00:01:11.822
- Okay, everybody, so when Cody
says so, let's loop our sounds.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:14.366
- Yes, please,
and then please stop looping

00:01:14.449 --> 00:01:16.869
when Christian and Hannah and I
stop singing. Got it?

00:01:16.952 --> 00:01:18.328
- ALL: Got it.

00:01:18.412 --> 00:01:20.330
- Oh, oh, and everybody
watching at home,

00:01:20.414 --> 00:01:22.249
feel free to clap along, huh?

00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:25.627
Okay, start us off, Benjamin.

00:01:25.711 --> 00:01:27.713
- (beatboxes)

00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:29.548
- Daniel, go!

00:01:29.631 --> 00:01:33.635
- (vocalizing)

00:01:33.719 --> 00:01:37.347
- All right, Andrew.
Come on in.

00:01:37.431 --> 00:01:44.605
- (vocalizing)

00:01:44.688 --> 00:01:46.815
- ♪ There are
lots of things we need ♪

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:50.068
♪ Even when we're mostly
staying at home ♪

00:01:51.737 --> 00:01:53.947
- ♪ And 100 kinds of work ♪

00:01:54.031 --> 00:01:57.326
♪ That would be difficult
to do on our own ♪

00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:03.540
- ♪ We need packages and mail,
need food on our plate ♪

00:02:03.624 --> 00:02:07.169
- ♪ We need medicine and care
when we're not feeling so great ♪

00:02:07.252 --> 00:02:09.796
- ♪ We need working electricity ♪

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.299
♪ So we can call our friends
on the phone ♪

00:02:12.382 --> 00:02:14.635
- ♪ And say we're not alone ♪

00:02:14.718 --> 00:02:18.388
- ♪ Somebody's out there
for me and for you ♪

00:02:18.472 --> 00:02:20.974
♪ Somebody who can run
to the trouble ♪

00:02:21.058 --> 00:02:22.601
♪ 'Cause that's what they do ♪

00:02:22.684 --> 00:02:25.646
♪ But don't worry,
you can do something too ♪

00:02:25.729 --> 00:02:28.857
- ♪ Sing a song
and say thank you ♪

00:02:29.775 --> 00:02:31.860
- ♪ Sing a song
and say thank you ♪

00:02:31.944 --> 00:02:33.320
- Thank you,
health care workers.

00:02:33.403 --> 00:02:35.697
- ♪ Sing a song
and say thank you ♪

00:02:35.781 --> 00:02:37.199
- Thank you, delivery people.

00:02:37.282 --> 00:02:39.284
- ♪ Sing a song
and say thank you ♪

00:02:39.368 --> 00:02:40.953
- Thank you, firefighters
and police officers.

00:02:41.036 --> 00:02:44.540
- ♪ Sing a song
and say thank you ♪

00:02:46.375 --> 00:02:49.044
- There are so many
other people I wanna thank too,

00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:51.380
like-like-like
transportation workers,

00:02:51.463 --> 00:02:53.090
and grocery workers,

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:56.885
and teachers and janitors
and volunteers and-and-and--

00:02:57.511 --> 00:02:59.304
- Well, I guess what
I'm really trying to say is,

00:02:59.388 --> 00:03:03.642
thank you to everyone who's keeping us
safe and happy and healthy.

00:03:03.725 --> 00:03:06.562
Oh, and a special thanks
to all the kids

00:03:06.645 --> 00:03:08.313
who are giving grown-ups
a helping hand.

00:03:08.397 --> 00:03:10.607
I am so proud of you.

00:03:10.691 --> 00:03:13.026
Now if you'll excuse me,
I'm gonna go see

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:14.778
if there are even more ways
I can help,

00:03:14.862 --> 00:03:17.531
and I hope you'll do the same.
Bye!

